cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this monograph in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Boundary Recovery Dynamics: Observability Defines Recoverability in Adaptive Neural Reconstruction"
authors:
  - family-names: Relational Intelligence Working Group
    given-names: ""
abstract: >-
  Canonical monograph on observability, recoverability, and boundary recovery
  dynamics in adaptive neural systems. The work formalizes the claim that
  optimization can only repair what observation can see, and that behavioral
  retraining can leave invariant boundary structure degraded in unobserved
  null-space coordinates.
version: 1.0.0
url: "https://github.com/Hexademic/boundary-recovery-dynamics"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hexademic/boundary-recovery-dynamics"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - observability
  - adaptive systems
  - invariant structure
  - boundary recovery
  - null space
  - representation geometry
